Heh. This reminds me of the probably-entirely-silly idea I've had
for a while about wallets.

A wallet is a thing which enables you to carry gold more
conveniently. I imagine that gold might weigh a bit more than it
currently does if you don't have a wallet, and less than it
currently does if you do.

Wallets occupy a `slot' on the player's body: you have to explicitly
start wearing one, at which point it belts on to your waist (or some
such) and all your main-inventory gold is then considered to be
contained in it. It doesn't function as a container in the general
sense that bags do: you can't (a)pply it. Also, when you remove a
wallet your money is all assumed to be taken back out of it: wallets
are never left lying around non-empty.

Wallets offer some protection against leprechaun robbing, probably
of the same probabilistic order as helmets do against mindflaying.
Perhaps a greased wallet would reliably protect you but the grease
would wear off (again like mindflaying).

In addition to the simple basic wallet, there are a number of fun
magical types:

 - Wallet of interest. This magically generates gold at a slow rate,
   provided you have some in there to begin with. The more you have,
   the more you get. Possibly there's a hunger cost or something to
   offset the effortless earning power.

 - Wallet of overdraft. This permits you to take out more than you
   put in: your main-inventory gold count can go below zero, and is
   capped at an overdraft limit of about -2000. (Perhaps -3000 or
   -1000 if it's blessed or cursed respectively.) There is
   definitely a noticeable hunger cost associated with having an
   overdraft active, and you can't remove even a non-cursed WoO from
   your wallet slot while it's overdrawn - you have to fill it back
   up to at least zero first. (However, creative methods of getting
   rid of it are fine, if you can somehow arrange to have it
   disintegrated or stolen by a nymph while overdrawn. I don't think
   the Kops have a fraud squad.)

 - Wallet of compulsive spending. Usually generated cursed (like
   GoFumbling, AoStrangulation or other nuisance items), so you
   can't take it out of your wallet slot. If you pick up any item in
   a shop which you have the funds to pay for, you automatically buy
   it instantly.

I'm sure this is a completely silly idea, and either destabilises
the game balance or is so pointless nobody would ever use any wallet
anyway. I'm not proposing it seriously. But the Wallet of Compulsive
Spending idea sprang almost fully formed into my head after I
returned from a real-life shopping trip with particularly poor self-
control, and I thought people here might at least be briefly
entertained by the rest :-)
